 "intro": "Use short everyday texts to find a time, a price, a place or a simple instruction.",
 "palabras": [
  {
   "palabra": "abierto",
   "significado": "open",
   "pron": "a-BYER-to",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "adjective",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "It agrees with what it describes: «el bar está abierto», «la tienda está abierta». B and v sound the same.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "cerrado",
   "significado": "closed",
   "pron": "the-RRA-do",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "adjective",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "The opposite of abierto. It changes with the noun: «el museo cerrado», «la tienda cerrada». The rr sounds strong.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "horario",
   "significado": "schedule, opening hours",
   "pron": "o-RA-ryo",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "noun",
   "genero": "m",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "It is used for shops, trains and classes: «el horario del tren». It ends in -o and is masculine.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "andén",
   "significado": "platform",
   "pron": "an-DEN",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "noun",
   "genero": "m",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "It has an accent on the last syllable: an-DEN. In the plural the accent disappears: «los andenes».",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "menú",
   "significado": "menu",
   "pron": "me-NU",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "noun",
   "genero": "m",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "It has an accent: me-NU. «El menú del día» is a full meal at a fixed price.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "precio",
   "significado": "price",
   "pron": "PRE-thyo",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "noun",
   "genero": "m",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "In Spain the c sounds «th»: PRE-thyo. You ask «¿Qué precio tiene?» or «¿Cuánto cuesta?».",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "salida",
   "significado": "departure, exit",
   "pron": "sa-LI-da",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "noun",
   "genero": "f",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "At a station it is the time the train leaves; in a building it is the door to leave by.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "mensaje",
   "significado": "message",
   "pron": "men-SA-he",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "noun",
   "genero": "m",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "It is masculine even though it ends in -e: «un mensaje nuevo». The j sounds like a strong h.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "cafetería",
   "significado": "café, cafeteria",
   "pron": "ka-fe-te-RI-a",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "noun",
   "genero": "f",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "«Café» + -ería = a café shop. The accent on í splits the vowels: «ka-fe-te-RI-a».",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "viernes",
   "significado": "Friday",
   "pron": "BYER-nes",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "noun",
   "genero": "m",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "The v sounds like b and «ie» is one syllable: «BYER-nes». Days are lowercase and have no plural change.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "abiertas",
   "significado": "open (feminine plural)",
   "pron": "a-BYER-tas",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "adjective",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "The «ie» is one syllable: «a-BYER-tas». It agrees with «puertas». The opposite is «cerradas».",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "muestra",
   "significado": "shows (mostrar)",
