   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Look for key information",
     "texto": [
      "A short notice often gives **one main piece of information**: a time, place, price or rule.\n\n- Read **the heading and the numbers** first.\n- Then look at **the words around them**: «salida», «andén», «precio», «cerrado».\n- You do not need to understand every word to find a train time or pick a dish from the menu.\n\nExample: «Tren a Toledo: **salida 10:25**, **andén 3**» tells you **when** and **where**."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "gramatica",
     "titulo": "Times, days and prices",
     "texto": [
      "Notices repeat formulas that are easy to recognise:\n\n- The time: **a las** + number: **a las diez**, **a las seis**.\n- The days: **de lunes a sábado** (from one day to another). A fixed day: **los domingos**.\n- The price: number + **euros**: **doce euros**.\n- Abierto and cerrado: **abierto** if what you describe is masculine (el bar) and **abierta** if it is feminine (la tienda). Plural: **abiertos**, **abiertas**.\n\nTo give the state of a place you use **estar**: **está abierto**, **está cerrada**."
     ],
